title: Example - LIST word marker
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Lists

Live demo of vocab/lists. `LIST` is the `<ul>` wrapper; `SHORTCUTS`, `MARKERS`, `VOCABS` are named inline `<$list>` views, each baking a useful filter. Reuse any of them across tiddlers.

Each named-view marker (`SHORTCUTS`, `MARKERS`, `VOCABS`) is inline-mode so its body's `<li>...</li>` stays inline and renders as one `<li>` per iteration. The filter on each marker decides what gets iterated. Add your own named views by creating new markers tagged `vocab/lists` with their own filter.

!! Demos

* [[Example - LIST SHORTCUTS]]. Iterates configured keyboard shortcuts.
* [[Example - LIST MARKERS]]. Iterates every custom-markup marker.
* [[Example - LIST VOCABS]]. Iterates every shipped vocabulary.

!! Related

* [[Customized Wikitext Lists]]. The marker schema and pragma-form alternative.

